        <title type="html"><![CDATA[fix outdated Safari compatibility note for `appearance: none`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39876</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39876"/>
        <updated>2025-06-09T18:32:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177649063?u=4c28e58bcd51210ed6392b4e108e698d7e19786f&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This PR updates the compatibility information for the CSS property <code class="notranslate">appearance: none</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Previously, the MDN note incorrectly stated that Safari does not support <code class="notranslate">appearance: none</code>. However, this limitation only applied to older versions of Safari. Modern Safari versions (from Safari 16 onwards) support it properly.</p>
<p dir="auto">This correction improves the accuracy of the documentation and ensures developers are not misled by outdated notes.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarified that Safari 16+ removed styling restrictions on , allowing appearance: none; for flexible styling.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The previous documentation was outdated regarding Safari's behavior. This update improves accuracy and helps developers style search inputs consistently.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-16-release-notes" rel="nofollow">Safari 16 Release Notes</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



]]></content>
